{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A wise man went up against a city of mighty men</b> — to teach that wisdom is better than might." "<b>might</b> — an allusion to the walls, as in the verse: \"until your walls come down\"." "<b>its trust</b> — for the mighty men trusted in it."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:01.109845270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}